---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="hero-pill">
        <span class="status-dot"></span>
        <span>AI consultancy for local business</span>
      </div>

      <h1>
        Practical AI that helps your business <em>save money</em> — not chase hype.
      </h1>

      <p>
        Eight34 Labs helps shops, restaurants, offices, and service businesses find the few places AI genuinely cuts costs and hours — then sets it up for you, trains your team, and stays nearby in Ridgewood, New Jersey.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 10px 22px; font-size: 14px;">
          Contact Us →
        </a>
        <a class="btn-outline" href="/services" style="padding: 10px 22px; font-size: 14px;">
          See what we set up
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Trust chips -->
    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">START LOCAL</span>
          <h3>Start local</h3>
          <p>Ridgewood first, then Bergen County, then NJ</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">PLAIN ENGLISH</span>
          <h3>Plain English</h3>
          <p>No jargon, no lock-in, no overselling</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">DONE WITH YOU</span>
          <h3>Done with you</h3>
          <p>We configure it — you keep control</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What we do -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>What we do</h2>
        <p>Find the waste. Automate the boring parts. Keep the human parts human.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-500); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        Most small businesses don&rsquo;t need an &ldquo;AI strategy.&rdquo; They need someone to look at the weekly grind — inbox, scheduling, invoices, follow-ups, inventory — and quietly remove the hours that shouldn&rsquo;t be there.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">01 · AUDIT</span>
          <h3>AI Opportunity Audit</h3>
          <p>We sit with you, map how work actually flows through your business, and rank the spots where AI saves real time or money — including the honest answer &ldquo;not worth it&rdquo; where it applies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">02 · SETUP</span>
          <h3>Setup &amp; Integration</h3>
          <p>We choose tools that fit your budget and your existing software, connect them, and configure them properly — inboxes, booking, documents, customer questions, back-office tasks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">03 · SUPPORT</span>
          <h3>Training &amp; Ongoing Help</h3>
          <p>Your team learns the new workflow in plain language, with simple guides. Then we check in, tune what&rsquo;s not working, and add the next improvement only when the first one is paying off.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 28px;">
        <a class="btn-outline" href="/services" style="padding: 10px 22px; font-size: 14px;">Explore services in detail →</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Why local -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Why local, why now</h2>
        <p>Big firms sell platforms. We sit at your counter.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-500); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        AI tools got cheap and capable fast — but the setup is where local businesses lose. Wrong tool, wrong settings, no training, and it becomes one more subscription nobody uses.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">IN-PERSON</span>
          <h3>In-person where it matters</h3>
          <p>Based in Ridgewood — we can be at your shop, not on a sales call three time zones away.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">YOUR TOOLS</span>
          <h3>Built around your tools</h3>
          <p>We work with the email, calendar, point-of-sale, and software you already pay for.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">SAVINGS FIRST</span>
          <h3>Savings first, technology second</h3>
          <p>Every recommendation has to name the hours or dollars it gives back — or we don&rsquo;t recommend it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Explore index -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150);">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Explore Eight34 Labs</h2>
        <p>Everything else, in full.</p>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size: 15px; color: var(--ink-500); max-width: 600px; margin-bottom: 40px;">
        The short version is above. The full picture — what we set up, how we work, where we work, and who is behind it — lives on these pages.
      </p>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">SERVICES</span>
          <h3>What we set up</h3>
          <p>Every service in detail, what a first project actually includes, the worksheet to size up your own busywork, and straight answers to the questions owners ask us.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><a href="/services" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-950);">Go to Services →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">PROCESS</span>
          <h3>How we collaborate</h3>
          <p>Phase by phase: what happens, what you get, what we need from you, and what working together looks like week to week — before, during, and after setup.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><a href="/process" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-950);">Go to Process →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">LOCAL FOCUS</span>
          <h3>Where we work</h3>
          <p>Why we start in Ridgewood, the Bergen County businesses we are built for, how the county rollout works, and what comes next across New Jersey.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><a href="/local" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-950);">Go to Local Focus →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">ABOUT</span>
          <h3>Who is behind it</h3>
          <p>Meet Tee Jay, how Eight34 grew from a web engineering studio into an AI consultancy, the principles we work by, and how we measure whether any of this is working.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><a href="/about" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-950);">Go to About →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="num">CONTACT</span>
          <h3>Start a conversation</h3>
          <p>What to tell us, what happens after you reach out, how to prepare for a first conversation, and the fastest way to get a reply from Tee Jay.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 16px;"><a href="/contact" style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-950);">Go to Contact →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="section" style="border-top: 1px solid var(--ink-150); padding-bottom: 90px;">
      <div class="contact-cta-box">
        <h2>No pitch deck. No pressure.</h2>
        <p>Start with a conversation about where your week actually goes.</p>
        <div class="contact-cta-actions">
          <a class="btn-primary" href="/contact" style="padding: 12px 24px; font-size: 14.5px;">
            Contact Us →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
